  "verdict": "7 of 11 reported 'predictions' are right-censored: the node never recovered inside its window, so the harness substituted the window length, which is a hand-set field. Ranking the events by that field alone \u2014 with no engine at all \u2014 reproduces the headline to 0.8717 against the engine's 0.8828. The engine adds +0.0110. On the 4 events where it genuinely reached recovery in-window, Spearman is 0.8000 at n=4, which supports nothing. The recovery-ordering result CANNOT be claimed as evidence of model skill in its present form.",
